cat > resources/fieldwork_note.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Larchmont Plus survey: fieldwork note

- Method: face-to-face interviews at store entrances, 7-19 September 2026, 8 stores, 10:00-19:00.
- Interviews per store set in proportion to each store's average weekly footfall:

| Store | Weekly footfall | Interviews |
|---|---|---|
| Larchmont Central | 21,000 | 149 |
| Quayside | 15,500 | 110 |
| Elm Park | 12,800 | 91 |
| Northgate | 11,200 | 80 |
| Ashby Road | 9,400 | 67 |
| Millbrook | 8,300 | 59 |
| Fenwick | 6,900 | 49 |
| Coleridge Sq | 4,900 | 35 |

- Completed interviews: 640. Margin of error for a proportion: +/-3.9 points at 95% confidence.
- Concept card shown: "Larchmont Plus: unlimited next-day home delivery on orders over GBP 25, GBP 4.99 a month, cancel any time."
- Question: "If Larchmont Plus were available, how likely would you be to join?" (5-point scale)
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
cat > resources/business_case.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Larchmont Plus: business case (draft for exec committee)

## Demand
- Survey: 41% of shoppers interested (definitely/probably would join).
- Customer base: 182,000 loyalty cardholders.
- Conservative haircut: assume only half of interested shoppers join.
- Members: 182,000 x 41% x 50% = **37,310**

## Economics (annual)
- Price: GBP 6.99/month.
- Delivery and picking cost per member: GBP 3.10/month.
- Fixed cost (12 vans on 3-year lease, drivers, routing software): GBP 1,200,000/year.
- Break-even members: 1,200,000 / ((GBP 6.99 - GBP 3.10) x 12) = **25,707**

## Recommendation
Members exceed break-even by 45%. Sign the van lease and launch in January.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
